WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.000
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.675
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:16.273
Unit thirty-three: Past Habits (would / used to). Today you will talk about what you did regularly in the past.

4
00:00:16.573 --> 00:00:19.237
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.595
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.416
Used to.

7
00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:28.799
Used to means a past habit or state.

8
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:30.617
I used to live there.

9
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.532
Your turn. Say: Used to.

10
00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:37.298
Used to.

11
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:38.680
Would.

12
00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:41.950
Would means a repeated past action.

13
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:44.166
We would visit every summer.

14
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.891
Your turn. Say: Would.

15
00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:50.583
Would.

16
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.409
Past state.

17
00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:56.461
Past state means a situation, not an action.

18
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.446
I used to be shy.

19
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.911
Your turn. Say: Past state.

20
00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:05.919
Past state.

21
00:01:06.683 --> 00:01:07.882
Past action.

22
00:01:08.883 --> 00:01:11.289
Past action means something that was done.

23
00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:13.279
We would go fishing.

24
00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:17.325
Your turn. Say: Past action.

25
00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.388
Past action.

26
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.221
Regularly.

27
00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.820
Regularly means often, at fixed times.

28
00:01:27.417 --> 00:01:28.754
We met regularly.

29
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:32.095
Your turn. Say: Regularly.

30
00:01:34.933 --> 00:01:36.027
Regularly.

31
00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:37.819
Contrast.

32
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:41.896
Contrast means a difference between past and now.

33
00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:44.297
A contrast with today.

34
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:47.838
Your turn. Say: Contrast.

35
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.840
Contrast.

36
00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:53.538
Nostalgia.

37
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.293
Nostalgia means a warm longing for the past.

38
00:01:57.883 --> 00:01:59.581
Nostalgia for childhood.

39
00:02:00.183 --> 00:02:02.708
Your turn. Say: Nostalgia.

40
00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:06.684
Nostalgia.

41
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.544
No longer.

42
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.654
No longer means not any more.

43
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.623
I no longer play.

44
00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:17.473
Your turn. Say: No longer.

45
00:02:20.333 --> 00:02:21.381
No longer.

46
00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:25.562
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:29.624
Visal, what did you use to do and would do as a child?

48
00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:41.171
When I was a child I used to live in a village, and every summer we would visit my grandparents. Used to and would both describe past habits.

49
00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:43.621
What is the difference?

50
00:02:44.717 --> 00:02:59.492
Used to works for both actions and states: I used to be shy; I used to have a dog. Would works only for repeated actions: We would swim every afternoon. We cannot say I would be shy.

51
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:01.875
Any other points?

52
00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:16.807
The negative is didn't use to. Would needs a time frame already clear in the context. These forms often show contrast with the present or nostalgia: I used to play football, but I no longer have the time.

53
00:03:17.967 --> 00:03:19.873
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.717 --> 00:03:24.284
Grammar focus: Past habits: used to and would.

55
00:03:24.584 --> 00:03:25.817
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.517 --> 00:03:27.994
I used to be very shy.

57
00:03:28.883 --> 00:03:31.324
Every summer we would visit my grandparents.

58
00:03:32.217 --> 00:03:33.938
I didn't use to like fish.

59
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:42.512
Used to = past habits and states. Would = repeated actions only (not states). Negative: didn't use to.

60
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.075
Be careful! Don't say: I would be shy as a child.

61
00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.799
Say: I used to be shy as a child.

62
00:03:52.099 --> 00:03:53.739
Would is not for states.

63
00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:57.174
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:57.967 --> 00:03:58.991
Looking Back.

65
00:03:59.291 --> 00:04:02.568
When I was a child, I used to live in a small village.

66
00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:06.193
Every summer we would visit my grandparents.

67
00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.488
I used to be shy, but now I enjoy speaking in public.

68
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.755
We would swim in the river every afternoon.

69
00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:17.532
I no longer live there, but I feel nostalgia for it.

70
00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:22.740
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:26.282
I blank be afraid of dogs. (state)

72
00:04:26.582 --> 00:04:29.957
A, would. B, used to. C, am used to.

73
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.743
The answer is B: used to.

74
00:04:36.883 --> 00:04:39.173
Every Sunday we blank go to the market.

75
00:04:39.473 --> 00:04:42.581
A, would. B, used to be. C, were.

76
00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.156
The answer is A: would.

77
00:04:49.317 --> 00:04:50.747
Which cannot use would?

78
00:04:51.047 --> 00:04:56.872
A, I used to have a bicycle.. B, We would play in the park.. C, We would visit them..

79
00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:03.780
The answer is A: I used to have a bicycle..

80
00:05:04.917 --> 00:05:06.812
The negative of used to is blank.

81
00:05:07.112 --> 00:05:11.926
A, didn't use to. B, not used to. C, didn't used to.

82
00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:17.733
The answer is A: didn't use to.

83
00:05:18.883 --> 00:05:21.220
According to the reading, where did they swim?

84
00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.301
A, in the river. B, in the sea. C, in a pool.

85
00:05:28.867 --> 00:05:30.704
The answer is A: in the river.

86
00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:35.040
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:35.883 --> 00:05:39.531
Write two sentences about what you used to do and would do as a child.

88
00:05:48.317 --> 00:05:49.747
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:50.047 --> 00:06:03.523
As a child I used to live near the river, and every afternoon we would swim there. I used to be afraid of deep water, but I no longer feel that way. These forms show my past habits.

90
00:06:03.823 --> 00:06:05.555
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:11.030
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past habits: used to and would.

92
00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:15.631
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:15.931 --> 00:06:18.676
See you in Unit thirty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:18.976 --> 00:06:22.418
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

